# Specify - Agent Instructions

This repository is the Specify **Rust runtime** plus ultrathin Cursor `/spec:*` skill wrappers. Domain generation lives in target adapters in [`augentic/specify-adapters`](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters).

## Vocabulary

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#vocabulary).

## Operating Model

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#workflow-overview). Specify owns the workflow contract; adapters contribute specialist analysis, generation, enrichment, and review behavior on top of that contract.

Operators drive phases with `/spec:*` skills (ultrathin invoke-and-relay wrappers over CLI verbs). **Engineering standards** live in rules (`codex/rules/` and per-adapter `prose/rules/` overlays); **authoring standards** live in [`docs/standards/`](../../docs/standards/). See [standards layer](../../docs/explanation/standards-layer.md).

## Main Inputs

1. **TypeScript → Rust WASM**: reconstruct baseline specs and design from an existing service.
2. **Manual → Crux App**: generate cross-platform Crux applications (Rust core, iOS shell, Android shell, design system).

## Authority Hierarchy

When conflicts arise, follow this strict precedence order:

1. **Specify artifacts** - `proposal.md`, `spec.md`, `design.md`, `tasks.md` (Vectis also: `tokens.yaml`, `assets.yaml`; `composition.yaml` is a target build output, not a Specify artifact)
2. **Guest orchestrations and embedded prompts** - `crates/slice/prompts/`, `crates/change/prompts/`, and the CLI single-writer contract
3. **docs/reference/**, **docs/standards/** (authoring house style — not engineering standards), and **sources/`<name>`/prose/prompts/** / **targets/`<name>`/prose/prompts/** in specify-adapters (+ each adapter's local `references/`) - authoritative patterns and examples
4. **`SKILL.md` wrappers** - argument elicitation and CLI invoke/relay only; never generation or orchestration rules
5. **Evidence** - source-extracted material; reference for ambiguity only
6. **LLM inference** - only after explicit evidence; prefer `[unknown]`

For `spec.md` requirement disagreements (the closed `authority` enum and its resolution order), see [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#authority-and-reconciliation-mechanics) and [synthesis/authority.md](../../crates/slice/prompts/synthesis/authority.md); for the adapter contract, see [docs/explanation/adapter-anatomy.md](../../docs/explanation/adapter-anatomy.md).

**Key principle**: If artifacts conflict with source, trust the artifacts. If artifacts are incomplete, mark unknowns rather than guessing.

## Artifact Boundaries

See [docs/explanation/artifacts.md](../../docs/explanation/artifacts.md) for the per-artifact responsibility breakdown and [docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md](../../docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md) for the specialist-vs-artifact dividing line (behavioral specs stay platform-neutral; target-specific detail lives in adapter prompts and references, not `spec.md`).

## Operator skills

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#skill--cli-responsibility-split) for the skill / CLI responsibility split. Per-skill detail (description, argument hints, body) lives under `plugins/<plugin>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`. Operators invoke these as `/spec:*` (and `/capture:*`) slash commands.

## Repository Layout

See [docs/reference/directory-layout.md](../../docs/reference/directory-layout.md) for the full directory structure. Key directories:

```text
/.cursor/rules/           # Project guidance for agents
/.cursor-plugin/          # Multi-plugin marketplace manifest
/docs/                    # Extended documentation (explanation, contributing)
/plugins/
  ├── spec/               # Specify workflow plugin (init, plan, refine, build, merge, finalize, drop)
  └── capture/            # Runtime capture plugin (wiretap / migration capture)
/src/, /crates/           # specify runtime binary and workspace crates
/tests/                   # Lightweight checks package (boundaries, links), fixtures/, fs_git.rs
/harness/                 # Fixture adapter, WASM boundary smoke, and the explicit live-model test
```

Shared codex rule packs (`codex/rules/universal/`, the `UNI-*` engineering rules) live in [`augentic/specify-adapters`](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters) alongside the adapter trees.

Source and target adapter trees (guest crates + `prose/prompts/`, per-adapter `prose/rules/` overlays, and the `codex/references/` prose embedded into components) live in [`augentic/specify-adapters`](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters).

## Validation

```bash
cargo test -p checks   # adapter boundary + docs/plugin link integrity
make ci                # the full Rust workspace gate (cargo make ci)
```

The `checks` package is plain cargo tests at `tests/` — only a Rust toolchain is required. They run inside `cargo make ci` with the rest of the workspace suite.

Test placement, the three rungs (native / WASM boundary / explicit live trial), and assertion ownership are defined in [`docs/standards/testing.md`](../../docs/standards/testing.md). The contributor-facing gate model is [`docs/contributing/quality-gates.md`](../../docs/contributing/quality-gates.md). Generic model/runtime mechanics belong to `omnia-testkit`; Specify owns only workflow scenario content — fixture leads, evidence, scripted answers, and assertions.

For generated crates in downstream consumer projects, the normal verification commands apply:

```bash
cd crates/<name> && cargo check
cd crates/<name> && cargo test
cargo build --target wasm32-wasip2 --release
cargo fmt -- --check
cargo clippy -- -D warnings
```

## Code Style And Constraints

### Microsoft Pragmatic Rust Style

- Strong typing with newtypes
- Explicit error handling
- Clear, descriptive naming
- Prefer small functions and explain genuinely complex logic

### Markdown style

- Do not hard-wrap prose in Markdown files solely for column width. Keep paragraphs and list-item prose on a single line unless the line break is semantically meaningful.
- Preserve intentional line breaks in frontmatter, tables, lists, blockquotes, and fenced code blocks.

### WASM And Omnia SDK Constraints

See [guardrails.md](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters/blob/main/targets/omnia/references/guardrails.md) for forbidden crates and APIs, provider trait rules, validation placement, and runtime constraints.

## File Locations

In downstream consumer projects:

- **Crates**: `$PROJECT_DIR/crates/<crate_name>/`
- **Metrics**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.metrics.json` when tracking is enabled

In this repository:

- **Working artifacts**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.specify/slices/<slice-name>/` (with per-source evidence at `evidence/<source>.yaml`)
- **Baseline specs**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.specify/specs/`
- **Plan + discovery**: `$PROJECT_DIR/{change.md,plan.yaml,discovery.md}` — operator-facing platform artifacts at the project root, alongside `registry.yaml` (workspace mode places these at the workspace root)

## Troubleshooting

### Artifact Issues

- Mark uncertain behavior with `[unknown]`; mark authority-resolved disagreements with `[divergence]`; mark unresolvable same-authority disagreements with `[conflict]`. Tags never park the slice — the lifecycle still transitions to `refined`.
- Keep specs behavioral and technical detail in `design.md`
- Review `docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md` when artifact responsibilities feel blurred

### Generation Issues

- Check the bound target adapter's `build` / `guidance` prompts first
- Review Omnia or Vectis references in specify-adapters for target and provider patterns
- Compare against worked examples before inventing a new pattern

## Skill wrappers

Wrappers stay ultrathin invoke-and-relay — no orchestration or generation prose. Frontmatter shape is the typed check in `tests/authoring.rs` (the `checks` package). See [docs/contributing/checks.md](../../docs/contributing/checks.md) and [docs/contributing/operator-plugins.md](../../docs/contributing/operator-plugins.md).

## For Contributors

- Keep `/spec:*` skill bodies as invoke-and-relay wrappers; body style is guidance in [`docs/standards/cli-contract.md`](../../docs/standards/cli-contract.md).
- Changes to generation behavior belong in guest orchestrations or adapter prompts in `specify-adapters`, not in skill bodies.
- Keep the repo aligned with the Rust-first operating model in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

## Getting Help

- Review `docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md`
- Review the relevant `/spec:*` skill body only for invoke/relay steps
- Review `targets/omnia/prose/references/` in specify-adapters
- Review `targets/vectis/prose/references/` in specify-adapters
